KNOWNBUG: N5008 [class.base.init]/9.1 + [class.mem.general]/10 -- the
implicitly defined default constructor of a DERIVED class does not apply
the base class's default member initializers: `struct B { bool e =
false; }; struct D : B {}; D d;` leaves d.e nondet.  A direct object of
the base works, and an explicitly-defaulted `B() = default;` also works;
only the fully implicit constructor of a base under derivation loses the
NSDMI.  This is the root of the std::optional<std::string> residual
(cpp17_optional_string): _Optional_payload_base's `_M_engaged = false`
was dropped, making has_value() nondet.  Reduced with cvise on
cbmc-preprocessed source (5 essential lines).  Header-free; g++/clang++
runtime-verified.  Flip to CORE when fixed.
